<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Bicarbonate at a glance">
  <div><strong>Normal physiology</strong><span>Bicarbonate is a major extracellular buffer.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Two useful ions</strong><span>Sodium bicarbonate provides sodium + bicarbonate.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Dose matters</strong><span>Hydration use and high-dose loading are not the same thing.</span></div>
</div>

<div class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">THE CORE SCIENCE</p>
    <h2>Bicarbonate helps the body manage acid-base balance.</h2>
    <p>Carbon dioxide, carbonic acid, bicarbonate and hydrogen ions exist in a dynamic equilibrium. The lungs help regulate carbon dioxide, while the kidneys help regulate bicarbonate and hydrogen-ion handling.</p>
    <p>That makes bicarbonate part of everyday physiology, not just a sports-supplement ingredient.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">THE CHEMISTRY</span>
    <h3>CO<sub>2</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O ⇌ H<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub> ⇌ HCO<sub>3</sub><sup>−</sup> + H<sup>+</sup></h3>
    <p>Carbonic anhydrase helps this system move quickly between forms throughout the body.</p>
  </aside>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__split">
  <div class="bhd-page__split-media">
    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/5078599/pexels-photo-5078599.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1400" alt="Spoon holding a measured powdered ingredient" width="1400" height="950" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
